The BF16 Q/K/V packing geometry and the native FP32 state orientation are
transcribed from retained Infinity MIT sources:

  libs/infinity-v3/backends/libtorch/cpp/kernels/qwen35_kernels.cu
  revision c4c90b9
  SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
  pack_gdn_inputs: qkF32 [tokens*key_heads,256] with Q[0:128] then
  K[128:256]; BF16 V tail at 2*key_heads*128; alpha in
  [0,value_heads) and beta in [value_heads,2*value_heads) in the F32
  prepared gate row.

  libs/infinity-v3/backends/libtorch/cpp/kernels/flashinfer_gdn.cpp
  and libs/infinity-v3/backends/libtorch/cpp/models/qwen35_models.cpp
  revision c4c90b9
  SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
  Provider FP32 state is [batch,value_heads,value=128,key=128]; native
  resident state is [batch,value_heads,key=128,value=128]. The initial
  native state is transposed and optionally gathered through an int64 source
  map; the final provider state is transposed back by sequence position with
  no source gather.

No arithmetic is added. The two state exports copy uint32 payload bits
exactly. The pack export performs only the source BF16 round-to-nearest casts
for Q/K and the source BF16 copy for V; alpha and beta are copied as F32.

The four unchanged Candle GDN entrypoints are not present in this module. The
retained Candle MIT notice/license from the sibling native_gdn module is copied
unchanged into the build output as LICENSE.candle-MIT so attribution remains
available with every produced bundle.

No Torch, C10, ATen, Python, Triton, TVM-FFI, or FlashInfer runtime is linked.
No numerical parity, performance, or GPU-execution qualification is claimed.
